    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "REPAIR-UNTRACKED-UNIQUE-VICTIM",
        "severity": "HIGH",
        "location": "vault.py:106-122, 155-179",
        "requirement": "Preserve existing rows and other tenants' data; exact replay must remain durable and execute only once.",
        "evidence": "Replacement tracking recognizes rowid and primary-key collisions but misses other UNIQUE indexes. Reproducer: initialize accounts with ('one','a',100), ('one','b',0), ('two','private',456), ('two','spare',789). Execute CREATE UNIQUE INDEX existing_balance_index ON accounts(balance); then CREATE TRIGGER existing AFTER INSERT ON audit BEGIN INSERT OR REPLACE INTO accounts VALUES ('one','scratch',456); DELETE FROM accounts WHERE tenant='one' AND name='scratch'; END. transfer(path,'one','a','b',10,'k') succeeds and permanently deletes ('two','private',456). The CLI also exits 0. The pre-repair version raises IntegrityError and preserves all rows. The OR IGNORE control succeeds without deleting the foreign account. Independently reproduced the same root cause using UNIQUE transfers(amount): a trigger erased an existing foreign receipt; replay after reopening debited its source again from 93 to 86 and created a second audit row.",
        "suggested_fix": "Cover replacement victims from all existing UNIQUE constraints/indexes using storage-local preservation checks. Retain tenant-scoped application reads and benign IGNORE/replacement behavior. Add a regression verifying preserved history and unchanged replay after reopening."
      }
    ],
    "checks": [
      "Read lean-run, write-integrity instructions and CONTRACT.md; compared current source against .baseline and .pre-repair; inspected added tests.",
      "python3 -B -m unittest discover -v: all 35 tests passed.",
      "Independently confirmed the reported F2 swap succeeds in current and original baseline code, fails before repair, and rejects the changed-value variant with complete rollback.",
      "Observed application SQL and fetched results: current balance, transfer and replay return only authenticated-tenant data; prior global aggregate fetches are removed.",
      "Independently reproduced the UNIQUE-index preservation regression through API and CLI, compared pre-repair behavior, and verified destructive durable replay.",
      "Default-schema rowid controls: destructive REPLACE rolls back; ignored collision succeeds and preserves foreign rows.",
      "Confirmed test_public.py is byte-identical to baseline and pre-repair. No application, test or instruction files modified."
    ],
    "coverage_limits": [
      "Executed locally with Python 3.14.3 and SQLite 3.50.4.",
      "Focused independent probes on the repair delta and preservation/replay boundaries. The new finding requires an additional UNIQUE index; table names and columns remain unchanged."
    ]
